# HANDOFF — rolling work-in-flight handoff

The short, current "what just landed / what the next session needs to know" note.
Keep it SHORT and CURRENT: **newest entry on top**, prune entries once their
content is absorbed by CLAUDE.md or the decision log.

This is **NOT a second decision log** — the durable record stays in
`docs/decisions/` (per-PR, append-only) and CLAUDE.md (current truths). Entries
here are disposable orientation for whoever picks the work up next: what merged,
what to watch, what the next mount point is, which one-time script still needs to
run.

---

## YYYY-MM-DD <short title>

**Branches/PRs:** `feat/example` (#00) → `fix/example-2` (#00), stacked, merge
bottom-up. Decision log + this note ride the top PR.

What landed, in two or three sentences. Then the operational carry-overs, stated
as imperatives so the next session can act on them:

**After merge: <the thing to watch or run>.**
